examined trends in age-adjusted cocaine-involved and psychostimulant-involved death rates from 2003 to 2017\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Analyses comparing changes in death rates from 2016 to 2017\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Analyses comparing changes in death rates from 2016 to 2017 used z-tests when deaths were ≥100\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"were analyzed overall, and with and without any opioids and synthetic opioids, using Joinpoint regression.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Age-adjusted death rates were calculated by applying age-specific death rates to the 2000 U.S. Census standard population age distribution\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Z-tests were used if the number of deaths was ≥100, and a p-value of <0.05 was considered to be statistically significant.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Rates based on <20 deaths are not considered reliable and not reported.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"State-level analyses comparing death rates from 2016 to 2017 included 34 states and DC that met the following criteria\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"analytic_depth\"]}", "type": "text"}]}